    "title": "Evanston committee calls for Congress to ban federal agents from wearing masks - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By ABC7 Chicago Digital Team ,\n12 hours ago\nA resolution is moving forward in Evanston, calling on Congress to ban federal law enforcement agents from wearing face masks.\nABC7 Chicago is now streaming 24/7. Click here to watch The city's Human Services Committee passed a resolution on Tuesday night that now heads to Evanston City Council.\nThe resolution calls on the United States Congress and the Illinois General Assembly.\nChicago Mayor Brandon Johnson signed an executive order last weekend, also urging federals agents that may come to Chicago to not wear masks.\nREAD ALSO | Johnson signs order aimed at resisting planned immigration crackdown, possible Nat. Guard deployment\nThe Chicago executive order calls on federal law enforcement to follow municipal policies, including prohibiting officers from wearing masks to conceal their identities.\n14",
